    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, it isn't just my thoughts. it's the reality. the articles, the comments, the way my former colleagues won't even look me in the eye. i can't go back to being that person. that person doesn't exist anymore. it's like i'm a ghost walking around in a body that doesn't belong to me. how do you find hope when the entire world has already decided who you are and they've decided you're nothing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is understandable that when your past is viewed through the lens of others' judgment, it feels like a crushing, undeniable reality rather than just internal pain. However, remember that others' actions or lack thereof often reflect their own unhealed wounds rather than the true value of who you are. There is still a small, hidden part of you that deserves respect and safety, even if the world has momentarily forgotten to see it.",
